@inherits UiComponentBase

@* FloatingNav — Ruixen UI's floating navigation bar: a rounded bar of icon-and-label items with a
   soft pill that slides to whichever item is active, on upstream's spring (stiffness 400,
   damping 30).

   Upstream pins the bar to the bottom of the window itself, centred and fixed. Here the
   placement is the caller's, through Class, because a component that positions itself against
   the window cannot sit in a page, a card or a documentation example — the same reason the
   Sidebar examples need a frame. `Class="fixed inset-x-0 bottom-4 z-50 mx-auto"` is upstream's.

   The pill is in the markup before any script runs: the active item draws it inside itself, so
   a page with no script still shows where the reader is. ui.js lifts it out onto the bar and
   from then on moves that one element, measured against the item, on Motion's spring. *@

<nav data-slot="floating-nav" aria-label="@Label" class="@Classes" @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">@ChildContent</nav>

@code {
    /// <summary>Names the navigation landmark.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Label { get; set; } = "Main";

    // bg-background and the default border where upstream writes bg-white / dark:bg-neutral-900
    // and border-gray-200: the same white bar, from the theme.
    string Classes => Cn("relative flex w-full max-w-lg items-center justify-between rounded-full border bg-background px-1 py-2 shadow-xl", Class);
}
